tems of Real Madrid and Dreamland Gran Canaria, he also has the status of a quota, a valuable circumstance in the construction of the squad. In Bilbao, he will share the team's leadership with Harald Frey and Adam Somogyi. Far from considering this coexistence as an individual battle for minutes, the Slovenian sees it as a competition designed to raise everyone's level. «I have a lot of hunger. We have to help each other, get the most out of each other and then whatever happens, happens,» he said. His path contains some parallels with the journey of Melwin Pantzar, who also came to Surne from a lower category before settling in the elite. Duscak coincided with him during his time in Madrid and acknowledges that his trajectory can serve as a reference for him. «He is a great example of effort. Even then, I realized that he was a great person. He can be a mirror for me because of his intensity and everything he has done,» he said. He therefore takes on the challenge of occupying a space marked by the Swedish player's good performance, although he intends to travel it with his own identity. «It's a challenge. Each one does their own thing and I will contribute everything I can. I want to give my all every day, both in games and in training. I like challenges,» he proclaimed. The Slovenian still observes the ACB with caution, as a 24-year-old player who is discovering a new scenario. He does not dare to measure the potential of Surne against rivals he still does not know, but he is left with a first impression: «Everyone wants to work and no one complains.» He was also surprised by the response from the squad. Several teammates wrote to him as soon as his signing became official, welcomed him and gave him their phone numbers to help him with whatever he needed. «I felt loved by the players, the coaching staff and everyone who works at the club.» Now, Miribilla awaits him, a much larger scenario than those he has frequented so far. The change does not intimidate him; on 